WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.250 --> 00:00:04.800
Supply Chain Control Tower. A 90-store retail network is missing its service target. Buy more stock, or move what it already has?

2
00:00:05.250 --> 00:00:11.800
On-time-in-full delivery sits at 90.4% against a 95% target.

3
00:00:12.250 --> 00:00:19.300
Every region misses. Split into its two failures, short-shipping, not lateness, is the bigger one.

4
00:00:19.750 --> 00:00:26.800
Over 13 weeks the replenishment gap grew 15.2% while stock on hand barely moved. The stock is in the wrong place.

5
00:00:27.250 --> 00:00:33.800
$96,330 of the gap is a transfer between warehouses, not a purchase order.

6
00:00:34.250 --> 00:00:42.300
A medallion pipeline with three defences, under an eight-page Power BI control tower.

7
00:00:42.750 --> 00:00:51.300
Each defence is proven by breaking the data on purpose: drift halts the run, bad rows are quarantined, a failure blocks publishing.

8
00:00:51.750 --> 00:00:58.300
Suppliers are scored on what they did: 18 of 24 sit in a different band than their contract says.

9
00:00:58.750 --> 00:01:05.300
A live studio turns a disruption into owned actions: in the Mexico scenario, 13 SKUs have no qualified alternate.

10
00:01:05.750 --> 00:01:11.800
Read the case study, or open the live decision studio. Run as a Databricks job, all 36 Gold measures matched the local pipeline to the cent. Synthetic data, labelled throughout.

